[38;5;252m[1m## What was found and fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The Rust translation was structurally complete — symbol parity was already 38/38 on the first [38;5;10mnm -D[0m comparison, in both directions, so no module was missing and no [38;5;10m#[no_mangle][0m wrapper had to be added. The bugs were all in [3mnumeric[23m fidelity:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m1. SSE operand-order / NaN-propagation divergences (real, fixed).[22m The C is compiled at [38;5;10m-O0[0m, so every float expression becomes one SSE instruction with a fixed dest/src assignment, and that assignment decides which NaN payload and [1msign[22m survives. LLVM legitimately commutes [38;5;10mfadd[0m/[38;5;10mfmul[0m and rewrites [38;5;10m-a*b + c[0m into [38;5;10mc - a*b[0m, which changed the answer. Two concrete divergences surfaced first:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mc2Dot({inf, NaN}, {-0.0, 3.4e38})[0m → C [38;5;10m0x7FC00000[0m, Rust [38;5;10m0xFFC00000[0m[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mc2MulrvT[0m with [38;5;10ma.s = NaN[0m → C [38;5;10m0xFFC00000[0m, Rust [38;5;10m0x7FC00000[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
I read the operand order for every arithmetic expression out of [38;5;10mobjdump -d[0m on the C [38;5;10m.so[0m and added explicit [38;5;10mfadd[0m/[38;5;10mfsub[0m/[38;5;10mfmul[0m/[38;5;10mfdiv[0m/[38;5;10mfneg[0m helpers that spell out the SSE rule (quieted dest if dest is NaN, else quieted src, else [38;5;10m0xFFC00000[0m on an invalid operation), then wired each call site in the order gcc actually emitted — including the non-obvious ones like [38;5;10mc2Add[0m's dest being [1m[38;5;10mb[0m[22m, and [38;5;10mc2CircletoCircle[0m's [38;5;10mA.r + B.r[0m having dest [1m[38;5;10mB.r[0m[22m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m2. Bounds-check panics where the C reads on (fixed).[22m [38;5;10mc2GJK[0m indexes [38;5;10mcache->iA[i][0m, [38;5;10mpA.verts[iA][0m and [38;5;10msaveA[i][0m with unvalidated values. Rust slice indexing would abort where the C keeps going, so those became raw pointer arithmetic mirroring the C.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m3. Three rows are UB-excluded, with evidence.[22m [38;5;10mc2MakeProxy[0m writes nothing for an unknown [38;5;10mC2_TYPE[0m, so [38;5;10mc2GJK[0m then reads the uninitialised [38;5;10mc2Proxy pA;[0m stack local — no defined value to match. And [38;5;10mcache->count >= 4[0m makes the C read [38;5;10miB[3][0m, which aliases the [1mfloat[22m [38;5;10mdiv[0m reinterpreted as an int ([38;5;10m1.0f[0m → [38;5;10m1065353216[0m), used to index [38;5;10mpB.verts[][0m; I compiled a plain C caller against the C [38;5;10m.so[0m and confirmed it dies with [38;5;10mSIGSEGV[0m. Negative counts are fully defined and [3mare[23m asserted.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
